body:
J02 delivers gpu/hwcodec/jpeg/{rwjpeg.c,rwjpeg.h,n2jpeg_hw_vt.c}. Integration proposal for gpu/video/vt/n2vt_shim.c (your file, not mine):

a) Add to the link: gpu/hwcodec/jpeg/rwjpeg.c and gpu/hwcodec/jpeg/n2jpeg_hw_vt.c, with -I gpu/hwcodec/include -I gpu/hwcodec/jpeg. They compile for arm64-apple-ios16.0 with the existing gpu/video/sdk headers and -nostdinc (verified). Needs libSystem ioctl (I declare it locally on __APPLE__, no sys/ioctl.h needed), open/close, malloc/free, pthread_* -- all already in the TBD set or libSystem.tbd.

b) Declare weak in the shim, exactly like n2avc_vt_create:
  extern OSStatus n2jpeg_hw_vt_create(uint32_t, CFAllocatorRef, VTVideoEncoderRef *) N2_WEAK;
  extern CFDictionaryRef n2jpeg_hw_vt_copy_registration_info(void) N2_WEAK;
  extern int n2jpeg_hw_vt_available(void) N2_WEAK;

c) JPEG registration order. Do NOT register both for jpeg by default: VideoToolbox keeps no per-frame fallback between registered encoders, so a plain jpeg client could get the software one. Proposed:
  if (access(N2VT_SWITCH_NO_JPEG, F_OK) == 0) state=off;
  else if (n2jpeg_hw_vt_available && n2jpeg_hw_vt_available()) {
      CFDictionaryRef info = n2jpeg_hw_vt_copy_registration_info ? n2jpeg_hw_vt_copy_registration_info() : NULL;
      jpeg = VTRegisterVideoEncoderWithInfo(jpeg, info, n2jpeg_hw_vt_create);
      if (info) CFRelease(info);
  } else if (n2jpeg_vt_create != NULL) {
      jpeg = n2_register_one(jpeg, N2STR(N2VT_ID_JPEG), n2jpeg_vt_create, claim_hw);
  }
n2jpeg_hw_vt_available() opens /dev/redwood-jpeg (0666) and checks RWJ_INFO abi==1 && caps bit0, so it is safe in every process. The hw objects info has CMClassImplementationID "com.nord2.videotoolbox.videoencoder.jpeg.mtk" and kVTVideoEncoder_IsHardwareAccelerated = true, so clients can also pick it explicitly.
d) The hw object is an exact behavioural mirror of gpu/video/vt/n2jpeg_vt.c (same property table, same Quality mapping, same NV12 path) plus BGRA input; on a device error it emits VTEncoderSessionEmitEncodedFrame(-12912) and returns -12912. It never emits a software frame.
e) Host test: if you want it, the VT object is tested against gpu/video/fake by gpu/hwcodec/jpeg/test_j02/run_tests.sh (78 checks x ASan/TSan/O2); no changes to gpu/video required.
Questions: (1) do you want the fallback-to-software registration above, or hw always registered plus software with a distinct ID? (2) is there an hw-ip build script I should call for the acceptance compile check, or is the gpu/video/build_ios.sh flag set the one to use?
